WEBVTT

title-1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.810
Loopback Transformer:

title-2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.510
Towards a Unified View of
Residual Looped Transformers.

memory-3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:10.220
Linear attention is a memory over tokens:

memory-4
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.960
each token writes its key
and value into a state,

memory-5
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.590
the state is passed along,

memory-6
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.960
and later tokens read from it.

memory-7
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.100
We apply the same write, transport
and read to depth:

memory-8
00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.560
each block writes its update
into the residual stream,

memory-9
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.800
and later blocks read the stream.

memory-10
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:31.660
Unrolled, every read is a
weighted sum of what was written;

memory-11
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.460
plain residual addition
fixes every weight at one.

knobs-12
00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:38.620
In this view,

knobs-13
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.080
every residual rule sets three things:

knobs-14
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.340
the input's strength,

knobs-15
00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.280
the total weight of the updates,

knobs-16
00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.140
and how that weight is shared.

knobs-17
00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.300
When the same blocks repeat,

knobs-18
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.300
plain addition lets the
total grow with every pass.

method-19
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.690
Loopback sets the three separately.

method-20
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.690
The input keeps weight
one on its own path,

method-21
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.390
a decay bounds the total,

method-22
00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.330
and attention shares it
across the stored updates.

live-23
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.940
Here a standard Transformer and Loopback,

live-24
00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.440
both at 3B scale,

live-25
00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.090
read the same new text.

live-26
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.340
Loopback is 23% smaller,

live-27
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.210
and its loss still ends lower.

scale-28
00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:21.460
From 191M to 3B parameters,

scale-29
00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.460
Loopback gets lower loss than the standard

scale-30
00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:27.200
Transformer with 40–75% of its parameters.

nine-31
00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.700
Against seven other looped designs,

nine-32
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.223
it has the lowest loss and the highest

nine-33
00:01:34.223 --> 00:01:37.060
benchmark average at all
three sizes we tested.

math-34
00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.390
And at 3B parameters,

math-35
00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.060
it more than doubles
word-problem accuracy,

math-36
00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:47.080
from 2.6% to 6.4%.

outro-37
00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.300
That's Loopback.

outro-38
00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.280
Fewer parameters,

outro-39
00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:53.180
lower loss.

outro-40
00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:55.580
The paper and code are
on our project page.
